---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import profilePicture from "../assets/profile-picture.jpg";
const pageTitle = "Bio";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <section>
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-4">
      <div class="w-full md:w-1/3 shrink-0">
        <Image
          src={profilePicture}
          alt="A photo of Justin Groves overlooking a lake."
          class="w-full rounded-full"
        />
      </div>
      <div
        class="flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center w-full md:w-2/3 gap-6"
      >
        <h2 class="font-logo text-4xl small-caps">Justin Groves, PhD</h2>
        <p class="tag-line">Sr. Data Scientist & Machine Learning Enthusiast</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
      <p class="tag-line">
        The Doctor is in.
        <sup id="ref-1">
          <a href="#fn-1" class="text-xs link">1</a>
        </sup>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Problem solving is a core part of my work, and currently that includes
      taking messy data and translating it into business solutions. I work
      across all facets of the data lifecycle including engineering, analytics,
      and modeling.
    </p>

    <h2>What Do I Do?</h2>
    <p>
      Currently I'm a Sr. Data Scientist with <a
        href="https://reefpointgroup.com/"
        target="_blank"
        class="link">ReefPoint Group</a
      >, a D.C. based government consulting firm. In my time I've worked
      extensively with Palantir Foundry and Microsoft Power Platform
      understanding the business needs of non-technical stakeholders and turning
      them into data-driven solutions for the VA.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some of my notable projects include building a classification model for
      detecting demographic collection points in VA forms and building out a
      full database management system (DBMS) with Microsoft Power Platform for
      tracking and analyzing
      <a href="https://pra.digital.gov/" target="_blank" class="link"
        >Paperwork Reduction Act (PRA)</a
      > collections as they move through the approval lifecycle.
    </p>

    <p>
      My background includes a PhD in mathematics from <a
        href="https://math.utk.edu/">The University of Tennessee - Knoxville</a
      > where I researched applications of <a
        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elliptic_curve">elliptic curves</a
      > to <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Error_correction_code"
        >error-correcting codes</a
      >. I also possess a minor in Data Science and Statistics.
    </p>

    <h2>Where Will I Be?</h2>
    <p>
      My goal is to continue to understand more of the data ecosystem. I aim to
      understand and implement cloud-based machine learning systems from
      end-to-end, getting the data out of the warehouses and into the hands of
      those who need it the most.
    </p>
    <p>
      There's no shortage of tools in the AI landscape, and I aim to leverage
      those for maximum efficiency. I continue to research and explore Natural
      Language Processing (NLP) and speech-to-text models (like Open AI's <a
        href="https://openai.com/index/whisper/"
        target="_blank"
        class="link">Whisper</a
      >) to extract insight from spoken word.
    </p>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
      <p class="tag-line">
        The future is now, and data is the key to the lock.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="my-8" />

    <ol class="text-xs">
      <li id="fn-1">
        Non-statistically significant results may vary.
        <a href="#ref-1" class="ml-2 link">↩</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
